---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Strength & Conditioning in Chiron — Support"
  description="Learn how to create and manage strength and physical therapy workouts in Chiron, including adding exercises, building your Exercise Library, and scheduling sessions."
>
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

      <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">
        <a href="/support-center" class="hover:text-primary-600">Support Center</a>
        <span class="mx-2">›</span>
        <span class="text-gray-700">Strength &amp; Conditioning in Chiron</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
        Strength &amp; Conditioning in Chiron
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-12">
        Chiron supports strength and physical therapy workouts alongside your run sessions, so your complete training load lives in one place.
      </p>

      <!-- Why S&C matters -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Why S&amp;C matters for endurance athletes</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          Strength and conditioning isn't optional for competitive runners — it's what keeps you healthy and fast across a full season. Targeted S&amp;C work builds the hip stability, posterior chain strength, and single-leg mechanics that translate directly to better running economy and fewer injuries.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Creating a workout in the Library -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Creating a strength workout in the Workout Library</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          The Workout Library is the best starting point for any session you'll repeat — a gym circuit, a pre-run activation, a physio protocol.
        </p>
        <ol class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 mb-6">
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">1.</span>
            <span>Navigate to the Library: <strong>Schedule → Add → Library Workout</strong>, or <strong>More → Workout Library</strong>.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">2.</span>
            <span>Tap <strong>Create Workout</strong> and set the activity type to <strong>Strength</strong> or <strong>Physical Therapy</strong>.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">3.</span>
            <span>Give the workout a name, then tap through to the <strong>Edit Exercises</strong> screen.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <figure class="mt-6">
          <img
            src="/images/support-center/strength-and-conditioning/chiron-edit-exercises-screen.png"
            alt="The Edit Exercises screen in Chiron showing the exercise list and Add exercise field"
            class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm mx-auto max-w-xs"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center">The Edit Exercises screen</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Adding exercises -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Adding exercises</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Tap the <strong>"Add exercise – type or search…"</strong> field at the top of the screen. You have two options:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong>Plain text</strong> — type the exercise as you'd write it in a training log, e.g. <em>RDL 4 x 8 @ 105kg</em>. The text is saved exactly as written. No category or muscle group data is attached unless you save it to the Exercise Library (see below).
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <div>
              <strong>From the Exercise Library</strong> — start typing a name to search existing exercises. Select one to add it with its category and muscle group data already attached.
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
          Once added, tap <strong>Add sets</strong> on the exercise card to configure sets, reps, and load.
        </p>

        <figure class="mt-6">
          <img
            src="/images/support-center/strength-and-conditioning/chiron-exercise-card.png"
            alt="An exercise card in Chiron showing the exercise name, category subtitle, Add sets button, drag handle and menu icon"
            class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm mx-auto max-w-xs"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center">Exercise card showing name, category, Add sets, drag handle, and menu</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Managing exercises -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Managing exercises</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <span><strong>Reorder</strong> — press and hold the drag handle on the left of any exercise card and drag to the desired position.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <span><strong>Edit / Modify structure / Delete</strong> — tap the three-dot menu on the top right of the exercise card.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Saving to the Exercise Library -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Saving an exercise to the library</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          To make a plain text exercise reusable, tap the three-dot menu → <strong>Save to library</strong>. On the next screen you can set:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <span><strong>Name</strong> — e.g. <em>Romanian Deadlift</em></span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <span><strong>Category</strong> — e.g. <em>Posterior Chain &amp; Hip Extension</em></span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <span><strong>Muscle groups</strong> — e.g. <em>Hamstrings</em>, <em>Glutes</em></span>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-6">
          Category and muscle groups are optional but useful for filtering and searching later.
        </p>

        <figure class="mt-6">
          <img
            src="/images/support-center/strength-and-conditioning/chiron-save-to-exercise-library.png"
            alt="The Save to Exercise Library screen in Chiron showing name, category and muscle group fields"
            class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm mx-auto max-w-xs"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center">Save to Exercise Library — set name, category, and muscle groups</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Saving the workout -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Saving the workout</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700">
          When all exercises are added, tap <strong>Save Exercises</strong> to save the workout to your Library.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Creating directly on the Schedule -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Creating a strength workout directly on the Schedule</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          If you want to build a one-off session without starting from the Library:
        </p>
        <ol class="space-y-4 text-gray-700">
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">1.</span>
            <span>On the Schedule, tap the date and add a new workout.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">2.</span>
            <span>Set the activity type to <strong>Strength</strong> or <strong>Physical Therapy</strong>.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">3.</span>
            <span>Add exercises using the same <strong>Edit Exercises</strong> flow above.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4">
          To reuse this workout in future, tap the three-dot menu on the workout → <strong>Save to Library</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Related articles -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related articles</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <a href="/support-center/scheduling-and-duplicating-library-workouts" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700 hover:underline">Scheduling and Duplicating Library Workouts</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <a href="/support-center/recording-a-strength-workout" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700 hover:underline">Recording a Strength Workout</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Back / Contact -->
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Need More Help?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
          Can't find what you're looking for? Get in touch with our team.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="/support-center"
            class="inline-block bg-white border border-primary-600 text-primary-600 px-8 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-primary-50 transition-colors"
          >
            Back to Support Center
          </a>
          <a
            href="/support-center/contact"
            class="inline-block bg-primary-600 text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-primary-700 transition-colors"
          >
            Contact Us
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
